  "contract_traces": [
    {
      "concern": "Required zero-speed stride endpoint",
      "proof": "AnimationLocomotionConfig owns required zero_speed_step_distance_metres: existing PositiveLength; canonical YAML explicitly supplies0.9. PositiveLength private finite-positive leaf/checked Deserialize and no serde default or fallback. ordinary_step_distance reads runtime owner, losslessly widens to NonnegativeLength, normalizes typed speed against positive walk endpoint and checked_lerps; above walk uses strictly ordered walk/run endpoints. No arbitrary ordering constraint imposed on endpoint distances. Whole-config YAML/default/validation/digest/snapshot/client-install receiver proof retained exact-hash from prior trace; no per-field manual transport projection is missing."
    },
    {
      "concern": "Positive speed widening and typed normalization",
      "proof": "From<PositiveSpeed> for NonnegativeSpeed is infallible subset widening. clamped_inverse_lerp accepts Into<Self> bounds, converts once, rejects lower>=upper before division, clamps exterior values to typed ZERO/ONE and admits interior checked quotient through canonical UnitInterval. No primitive overload, compatibility getter/alias or unchecked acceptance path is retained. All seven old nonnegative getter ports are migrated in actual delta, including melee typed integration and config ordering. SignedSpeed::nonnegative_part remains its distinct purposeful clamp."
    },
    {
      "concern": "Arithmetic owner and canonical Ratio",
      "proof": "NonnegativeSpeed subtraction yields finite SignedSpeed; multiplying it by UnitInterval cannot increase finite magnitude. Adding signed displacement re-admits finite/nonnegative arithmetic at existing speed owner. SignedSpeed division explicitly rejects zero and nonfinite quotient, returns existing fabelgeist_math::Ratio; UnitInterval TryFrom<Ratio> checks finite0..1. Canonical Ratio itself is unrestricted: no claim it guarantees finiteness or boundedness globally. SpeedError derives typed errors including ZeroDivisor/NonIncreasingBounds/Fraction; animation conversion maps bounds and retains quantity/cause distinctions."
    },
    {
      "concern": "Direct cubic and application retention",
      "proof": "UnitInterval::smoothstep uses direct x*x*(3-2*x), checked bounded admission and FractionResult; no reflected branch or shared raw adapter remains. All nine affected call sites propagate ? through existing typed error contracts. No proof of infallibility under floating point rounding or bitwise identity to prior reflected formula is asserted. Dive callers both guard phase>=DIVE_GROUND_CONTACT_PHASE; exact constant is HALF, admitted phase<=ONE, so local native rescale feeds interval0..1 before checked smoothstep. Direction native scalars are admitted once as BlendWeight and retained through checked_scale."
    },
    {
      "concern": "Height/gait/profile native receiving roles",
      "proof": "Final height007 authored compensation explicitly requires ordinary upright posture, correct pack/guard/ground/action gates; typed walk/run normalization supplies bounded scaling and moving fade is initial..positive blend. Config validates strict run>walk and blend>initial, so these authored operations cannot acquire zero/reversed spans from valid installed configuration. General locomotion profile keeps prone/supine/guard branches. Typed stride/reference speed/support cycle/bounce/flight/cadence and existing length/weight widening recipients carried from own earlier complete changed graph and actual final delta. No raw retained run fraction reintroduced."
    },
    {
      "concern": "Ownership, shape, derives and modules",
      "proof": "Existing UnitInterval, PositiveLength, NonnegativeLength, PositiveSpeed, NonnegativeSpeed, SignedSpeed, BlendWeight and math Ratio owners reused. Required locomotion field lives on existing extracted cohesive config owner; no duplicate ratio/fraction/length owner, parallel policy, Boolean payload split, compatibility API or redundant primitive config validation added. Leaf derives/checked Serde remain; aggregate validation only its support-cycle and ordered span relationships plus landing validation. Actual import/type/impl organization inspected in scoped files and prior unchanged-owner proof."
